[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-328592"] :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above.\nFind the unknown function $f(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))+\\text{i}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-333916/field-1/ce2978fa854528f38e1ed5f87209fd023cb3c23576b3fd5f4be76778c3c06f43" :answer/id #uuid "34a982aa-2379-5160-aadb-0e221bbe01c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sin(12t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333916/field-1/ba222d67897ad6203fa37da8c2ed8326dc67af6eb8b0a8d268b1ee1995808f8e" :answer/id #uuid "61c5d913-d230-57d2-8fa0-dabfd34182a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\sin(12t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333916/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e92f80b-24f0-5a62-95f7-57ffb2c0b02c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333916/field-1/ce2978fa854528f38e1ed5f87209fd023cb3c23576b3fd5f4be76778c3c06f43" :answer-field/choices ["q-333916/field-1/ce2978fa854528f38e1ed5f87209fd023cb3c23576b3fd5f4be76778c3c06f43" "q-333916/field-1/ba222d67897ad6203fa37da8c2ed8326dc67af6eb8b0a8d268b1ee1995808f8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333916/field-2/37336cdeed51b1b98defbb027e73eec970a67d2bf6a541cfde0de3783abcbb79" :answer/id #uuid "4c60452b-ee5e-5c06-bfaa-b6e3aa419816" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\cos(12t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333916/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "449749b2-fc95-5450-b01f-b347f4801903" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333916/field-2/37336cdeed51b1b98defbb027e73eec970a67d2bf6a541cfde0de3783abcbb79" :answer-field/choices ["q-333916/field-2/37336cdeed51b1b98defbb027e73eec970a67d2bf6a541cfde0de3783abcbb79"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333916" :question/id #uuid "57268f0c-de26-5f91-9b87-6de7da62058e" :question/math-academy-id "q-333916" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 18 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above.\nFind the unknown functions $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}g(t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n*Hint: One of the eigenvalues of the matrix is ${\\lambda }_{1}=12\\text{i}.$*\n\n$f(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,g(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 18 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe are given that the eigenvalue is ${\\lambda }_{1}=12\\text{i}.$ \n\nLet's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors. For ${\\lambda }_{1}=12\\text{i},$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-12\\text{i} & 18 \\\\ -8 & -12\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=12\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{12i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{12i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12t)+2\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)-3\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12t)+2\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12t)\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nf(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12t),\\,g(t)=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12t).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333916/field-1" "q-333916/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e3dd935-2058-5b28-bdbb-0c45586730d9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333916"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333909/selection/691717e80fb7966e72b003c126d1abebe437dec1b33c7072803522897105dc59" :answer/id #uuid "dd9fa2e0-c352-553a-bcdf-b84397a86a41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333909/selection/fdf9b0fd98ac4741d11254f96495abfc8e00bdb07ae6c069a0b54b7edc25dabf" :answer/id #uuid "725214f9-98b2-58ed-91ce-3b929cbef666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333909/selection/a074dae50edd42932432e0706147956add4acdf650317a06d2db149bb46e1fec" :answer/id #uuid "e0d45aa1-73af-5f49-a944-43fff8309bcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333909/selection/28308b2eba23afbd885bba49d89830ea831379aebdd3c18fded861b59886022e" :answer/id #uuid "a013a67e-7155-59f7-bfda-597aac7c721c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333909/selection/b9a4b5b064ac53f3d8a60a0a4bbff1fb6dbeacdc8c066b2229f343e8a6e26369" :answer/id #uuid "5c35146c-a057-5a87-8762-4aa0238ef72b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333909/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "556a23a3-a2ba-5074-90e1-f53ba2e6402c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-333909/selection/b9a4b5b064ac53f3d8a60a0a4bbff1fb6dbeacdc8c066b2229f343e8a6e26369" :answer-field/choices ["q-333909/selection/691717e80fb7966e72b003c126d1abebe437dec1b33c7072803522897105dc59" "q-333909/selection/fdf9b0fd98ac4741d11254f96495abfc8e00bdb07ae6c069a0b54b7edc25dabf" "q-333909/selection/a074dae50edd42932432e0706147956add4acdf650317a06d2db149bb46e1fec" "q-333909/selection/28308b2eba23afbd885bba49d89830ea831379aebdd3c18fded861b59886022e" "q-333909/selection/b9a4b5b064ac53f3d8a60a0a4bbff1fb6dbeacdc8c066b2229f343e8a6e26369"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333909" :question/id #uuid "e7848e39-87f6-5f74-a37b-941df8c79a27" :question/math-academy-id "q-333909" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above.\nFind the unknown function $f(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\text{i}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-333909/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e3dd935-2058-5b28-bdbb-0c45586730d9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333909"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333908/selection/0b282cac07d5f38b2bb3bf3b5bac5066ccc312cd13eb49382d177a2533c837d9" :answer/id #uuid "8ca793e9-bc51-51e0-b5d6-f10b57417348" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333908/selection/4b7a0167e0d8eb5ae892b4a6fd7c5bf37eaf630f8b53a170fc7d25bfde49057f" :answer/id #uuid "ee2a365b-cac6-5320-bbd4