ations above.\nFind the unknown function $f(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=3\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=3\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=3\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))+\\text{i}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-333908/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e3dd935-2058-5b28-bdbb-0c45586730d9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333908"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-329578/field-1/362bede28713d3197ad64f218eaeca6d1a474cd0ab03423f4e1040470371e970" :answer/id #uuid "c7e73afe-f47a-5b3f-8bca-a08c6153155d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sin(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186155291 :answer-field/correct "q-329578/field-1/362bede28713d3197ad64f218eaeca6d1a474cd0ab03423f4e1040470371e970" :answer-field/choices ["q-329578/field-1/362bede28713d3197ad64f218eaeca6d1a474cd0ab03423f4e1040470371e970"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-329578/field-2/e474d2085e67e5983f467f11639196a58aec5333fdb5bd20238a7ade909092a5" :answer/id #uuid "ba5b6ac7-3494-5685-a59a-1216275d474f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\cos(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186155292 :answer-field/correct "q-329578/field-2/e474d2085e67e5983f467f11639196a58aec5333fdb5bd20238a7ade909092a5" :answer-field/choices ["q-329578/field-2/e474d2085e67e5983f467f11639196a58aec5333fdb5bd20238a7ade909092a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-329578"] :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t).\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above.\nFind the unknown functions $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}g(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n*Hint: One of the eigenvalues of the matrix is ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}.$*\n\n$f(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,$\n\n$g(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe are given that the eigenvalue is ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}.$ \n\nLet's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors. For ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i},$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} & 1 \\\\ -1 & -\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nf(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,g(t)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-334063/selection/400c8db02d95f33997a78193fef673076b556631247cd1bc2f972a143be0eaaf" :answer/id #uuid "32771a8f-2a90-52bb-bad4-edbd7c8e08a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334063/selection/1e3861dd31d80e63da70394513ceccfa4fc0255ce2466c5a8b87a803785eafde" :answer/id #uuid "854d9ef9-627c-5e93-a220-59d0696580b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334063/selection/94d8272fdc3c8fdd77985bc02d2a190b16404e48d2b15250d2a0f2cebe715b99" :answer/id #uuid "a9a42a7c-7ebc-5f79-bb00-8c23700f11a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334063/selection/8c85a6166324aee2c181dd462fdcb5eaa31dcf8da91894cb5169599a6a3046d3" :answer/id #uuid "0787c17e-bc9f-56cf-8abc-1c5d2f310d43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334063/selection/e1cf0bbd3cdd0c54f0b97d5567e8dea0512bc1b9f948693d434431869fd0eaa1" :answer/id #uuid "60fe351a-c39a-5367-a787-1633dbe35045" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334063/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e29796e-67ad-5573-ba47-064742050095" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334063/selection/94d8272fdc3c8fdd77985bc02d2a190b16404e48d2b15250d2a0f2cebe715b99" :answer-field/choices ["q-334063/selection/400c8db02d95f33997a78193fef673076b556631247cd1bc2f972a143be0eaaf" "q-334063/selection/1e3861dd31d80e63da70394513ceccfa4fc0255ce2466c5a8b87a803785eafde" "q-334063/selection/94d8272fdc3c8fdd77985bc02d2a190b16404e48d2b15250d2a0f2cebe715b99" "q-334063/selection/8c85a6166324aee2c181dd462fdcb5eaa31dcf8da91894cb5169599a6a3046d3" "q-334063/selection/e1cf0bbd3cdd0c54f0b97d5567e8dea0512bc1b9f948693d434431869fd0eaa1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334063" :question/id #uuid "1230ef0c-2736-5f01-ab44-6913847462dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-334063" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 26 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=5\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-5\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 26 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=5\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-5\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=5\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1-5\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1-5\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-5\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-5\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t))+\\text{i}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =1[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]+0[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334063/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec2743cd-4e26-59d5-9368-7a77fa4d0527"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334063"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334053/selection/c6b5be669db51d0a65f11ec784ea3f4dc824c5da313be553d91b66a9856390ca" :answer/id #uuid "b40cfc1a-435b-5da5-9492-641be7200e71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334053/selection/48e2213956448a9de6b760365f2fdee415ff2a4ee897de2f3467538acd7c0ed5" :answer/id #uuid "da01089c-2bba-5fe0-9926-0b166dc152f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334053/selection/631832c679cb7654deff05d199d0798cd4a4620f1bfdc2881c56e6180e90cd82" :answer/id #uuid "36f69d04-eeb0-528a-8966-bdea6d6df63a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-13\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334053/selection/e89b3980fbd2b1a6822f1fca88b92ed3ca17a548c1f371a291d1f08add6d73c6" :answer/id #uuid "3aef1efb-5d13-592b-b3d6-895d84479414" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334053/selection/e99db41bf0ada17f4c0bf7039d380ba386898ada0b77eb0a27843185ab892bd8" :answer/id #uuid "6285f3bf-8b72-51ca-86c1-18e0cdfe8c8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334053/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "de7d054f-4d3f-52c6-9324-255ff9cd28c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334053/selection/631832c679cb7654deff05d199d0798cd4a4620f1bfdc2881c56e6180e90cd82" :answer-field/choices ["q-334053/selection/c6b5be669db51d0a65f11ec784ea3f4dc824c5da313be553d91b66a9856390ca" "q-334053/selection/48e2213956448a9de6b760365f2fdee415ff2a4ee897de2f3467538acd7c0ed5" "q-334053/selection/631832c679cb7654deff05d199d0798cd4a4620f1bfdc2881c56e6180e90cd82" "q-334053/selection/e89b3980fbd2b1a6822f1fca88b92ed3ca17a548c1f371a291d1f08add6d73c6" "q-334053/selection/e99db41bf0ada17f4c0bf7039d380ba386898ada0b77eb0a27843185ab892bd8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334053" :question/id #uuid "0f26b8b6-ea22-55f9-adb9-e96204409f88" :question/math-academy-id "q-334053" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}](\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\text{i}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =-[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-13\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334053/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec2743cd-4e26-59d5-9368-7a77fa4d0527"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334053"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334059/selection/d29fdc19dd3424c305695c16889507c31a41d9820470ca5f4bee4f9e6b62a88f" :answer/id #uuid "5292dc0c-7aa7-5eba-9637-c63659259286" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334059/selection/7b8d43e5e5889bbd05e3199420aa334f1582d6f46a3e292143e09be171bd83a1" :answer/id #uuid "31f424fb-e3c1-566c-b17d-f157decff9fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334059/selection/c10810e4030646670b066f30887e488f6ded4fcdbf050220a2af1bd12bdccb96" :answer/id #uuid "e216a835-3ccd-595c-b269-4ebd637c7595" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334059/selection/3ba7ee25fd707baa90634643ff703feb9132f792a24cdc3fff6072f165ea26ff" :answer/id #uuid "900b9aea-357c-5830-ab35-28bd6e1b02ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334059/selection/757fea1ce53c4920786ca0df7dc7d013ff10049160924e35907d3143891fff4f" :answer/id #uuid "009ad039-4818-57ce-9ad9-69185f94461a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334059/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "051548e1-5272-5718-acba-8071b327efcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334059/selection/757fea1ce53c4920786ca0df7dc7d013ff10049160924e35907d3143891fff4f" :answer-field/choices ["q-334059/selection/d29fdc19dd3424c305695c16889507c31a41d9820470ca5f4bee4f9e6b62a88f" "q-334059/selection/7b8d43e5e5889bbd05e3199420aa334f1582d6f46a3e292143e09be171bd83a1" "q-334059/selection/c10810e4030646670b066f30887e488f6ded4fcdbf050220a2af1bd12bdccb96" "q-334059/selection/3ba7ee25fd707baa90634643ff703feb9132f792a24cdc3fff6072f165ea26ff" "q-334059/selection/757fea1ce53c4920786ca0df7dc7d013ff10049160924e35907d3143891fff4f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334059" :question/id #uuid "67ecbe9d-e040-50e8-acb2-a8e956957fc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-334059" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 8 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=4\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 8 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=4\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=4\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))+\\text{i}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334059/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec2743cd-4e26-59d5-9368-7a77fa4d0527"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334059"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334058/selection/d3914bbecbfbbe6933e71360605fcbd6095ca388492e9e0b686a5555102e7b3d" :answer/id #uuid "bf133430-e75b-5d8d-8a9c-b21fea7dd6a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334058/selection/02f5e942c68bc72ee3d263eeb542ee96395d2e3a51ee5ed79840e5ecfc0f8db3" :answer/id #uuid "072601ab-6c31-5585-89f9-7f5891cc48f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{x}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334058/selection/9226af3a69f222d109f7e601d6209a802703c9664204dab92aae706c38b1e92f" :answer/id #uuid "6ee210e0-bfaf-5a6a-b298-076886e9bf32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334058/selection/b991f0aaebc29593d91501d23cad988fe762d580266ebcbd3c3891aa115aa7bc" :answer/id #uuid "9483f09e-3581-5707-a7ab-a2e1e2443d0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334058/selection/3fe859879d3e5a29718d0ec300a8a6db38ef0dd3a5743ad16421077f9ea0d610" :answer/id #uuid "76c23972-a758-5ee2-9439-dad8dc1f5048" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334058/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b247e3cc-ef1d-5a19-9b3a-6b7b15f98372" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334058/selection/02f5e942c68bc72ee3d263eeb542ee96395d2e3a51ee5ed79840e5ecfc0f8db3" :answer-field/choices ["q-334058/selection/d3914bbecbfbbe6933e71360605fcbd6095ca388492e9e0b686a5555102e7b3d" "q-334058/selection/02f5e942c68bc72ee3d263eeb542ee96395d2e3a51ee5ed79840e5ecfc0f8db3" "q-334058/selection/9226af3a69f222d109f7e601d6209a802703c9664204dab92aae706c38b1e92f" "q-334058/selection/b991f0aaebc29593d91501d23cad988fe762d580266ebcbd3c3891aa115aa7bc" "q-334058/selection/3fe859879d3e5a29718d0ec300a8a6db38ef0dd3a5743ad16421077f9ea0d610"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334058" :question/id #uuid "048c0890-2cea-5141-b151-d83b632a790f" :question/math-academy-id "q-334058" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\text{i}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\ 2{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =0[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334058/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec2743cd-4e26-59d5-9368-7a77fa4d0527"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334058"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334054/selection/6f494d35928a8827f64027534d51ecc9e263aa2abe5b90cbb859414647061791" :answer/id #uuid "08f9524f-fb76-5225-ab27-74448861f246" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334054/selection/91a663e67342b92eee987fbdd7fca89c7ead624d9c2e86abb81b2b6a767492d8" :answer/id #uuid "0b54f964-32d3-5846-bdfd-e84deecaca9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334054/selection/aaa3c307288c3b5b101f58956b4a7d0f6eaac3df0be64c884a164b11e60ea2d0" :answer/id #uuid "bea3e524-a5a4-5f89-aeff-25f9d1bc7c64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334054/selection/9698777f130decb9ddbb130d7691687bc7008fe21ccfe62aba19f522eef6a785" :answer/id #uuid "2036f215-1611-5a69-802b-f72da7ed8cbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334054/selection/adef4d6db417279976fd89bb1512e033b814d9a78429155ad3667026d61336c1" :answer/id #uuid "7258b1b7-265f-595d-bece-46ef942ce588" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334054/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "685eefa4-ce1b-55af-af15-3d4f19cb51f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334054/selection/adef4d6db417279976fd89bb1512e033b814d9a78429155ad3667026d61336c1" :answer-field/choices ["q-334054/selection/6f494d35928a8827f64027534d51ecc9e263aa2abe5b90cbb859414647061791" "q-334054/selection/91a663e67342b92eee987fbdd7fca89c7ead624d9c2e86abb81b2b6a767492d8" "q-334054/selection/aaa3c307288c3b5b101f58956b4a7d0f6eaac3df0be64c884a164b11e60ea2d0" "q-334054/selection/9698777f130decb9ddbb130d7691687bc7008fe21ccfe62aba19f522eef6a785" "q-334054/selection/adef4d6db417279976fd89bb1512e033b814d9a78429155ad3667026d61336c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334054" :question/id #uuid "b38a33fe-2eac-50c5-b2e0-e3e2d3c1ac54" :question/math-academy-id "q-334054" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=2\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2\\text{i}t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2\\text{i}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}](\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & =3[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334054/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec2743cd-4e26-59d5-9368-7a77fa4d0527"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334054"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334103/selection/5b30f4671c5d62fc7ff7d355bc17b6e023cd6892d3dd3b475396c0539fcbc379" :answer/id #uuid "541da5ac-12a0-54e5-8b6c-d4629508aaa6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334103/selection/08d30d22d053c306584dbad036a74552fdec3bcf663ecdb78e7ee695b94d6a04" :answer/id #uuid "7eae624b-642c-56e1-8ab6-3f08e764bfca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334103/selection/b535f7f49407bfbcbc8e413ce0ed16daf88c0e36857fc168b46f78a469e764e4" :answer/id #uuid "42a63f48-72c6-5731-9f79-2e1f9bb6009b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334103/selection/adea6de6de33b77366fb56ce5e7c5bea8e168241aa8eb80c0701b0fec906ee66" :answer/id #uuid "6dbb493c-1a93-5b05-aea1-fb71ade265ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334103/selection/30d8b5f7088639ad23e225c387052c84a6aed17222b971bddf29cbc1ade92045" :answer/id #uuid "02711d17-ce3b-56a5-93fb-cb0086015f28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334103/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "03c0633a-1d2c-5d91-97ad-35dd51c82fd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334103/selection/adea6de6de33b77366fb56ce5e7c5bea8e168241aa8eb80c0701b0fec906ee66" :answer-field/choices ["q-334103/selection/5b30f4671c5d62fc7ff7d355bc17b6e023cd6892d3dd3b475396c0539fcbc379" "q-334103/selection/08d30d22d053c306584dbad036a74552fdec3bcf663ecdb78e7ee695b94d6a04" "q-334103/selection/b535f7f49407bfbcbc8e413ce0ed16daf88c0e36857fc168b46f78a469e764e4" "q-334103/selection/adea6de6de33b77366fb56ce5e7c5bea8e168241aa8eb80c0701b0fec906ee66" "q-334103/selection/30d8b5f7088639ad23e225c387052c84a6aed17222b971bddf29cbc1ade92045"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334103" :question/id #uuid "f345db86-4fa2-5aaf-98e1-0020feb0363b" :question/math-academy-id "q-334103" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above.\nFind the unknown function $f(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ f(t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}\n$$\n\n*Hint: One of the eigenvalues of the matrix is ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+\\text{i}.$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given that the eigenvalue is ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+\\text{i}.$ \n\nLet's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors. For ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+\\text{i},$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} & 1 \\\\ -1 & -\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(4+\\text{i})t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(4+\\text{i})t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\text{i}({e}^{4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\text{i}({e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t} \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334103/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3692fa3-14c5-5db9-8fee-e99ae35e386f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334103"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-328595"] :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above.\nFind the unknown function $f(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}\n$$\n\n*Hint: One of the eigenvalues of the matrix is ${\\lambda }_{1}=1+2\\text{i}.$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given that the eigenvalue is ${\\lambda }_{1}=1+2\\text{i}.$ \n\nLet's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors. For ${\\lambda }_{1}=1+2\\text{i},$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=1+2\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(1+2\\text{i})t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(1+2\\text{i})t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}(2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t} \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-334126/selection/c2c4bf203f1457c081aa67df90b16554bb5c4e724fe5cea01dd9dc527aee883c" :answer/id #uuid "41811ccf-5ef9-5bb1-a37c-b667071da03b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334126/selection/bfdc395819ce23330ffd2d6f3b03d819bbd0860f564964e1b7470932594ec907" :answer/id #uuid "f7849968-14ed-58e7-85ed-cf26a7dda75b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)+15\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334126/selection/8d3e4dcc5745a1238e60616cb78b2a41cc363aa802ed60ae2d5c20912b398a6b" :answer/id #uuid "b1335884-5707-5068-bfd9-a238aeecb73d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334126/selection/bff161a2190bc6242a069ed224220089d10cb2d031d0e07863dd7f53bcda2984" :answer/id #uuid "152e4961-88b5-53c4-8fab-fa9e8a0db282" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334126/selection/7a20def5811c2ee4e0f2a9977ea59d1a32d066cbcd86b924fdee15c4c0b08a64" :answer/id #uuid "a03c9f47-52dd-5cdc-96da-fed3ce763f97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334126/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "beeb7142-5036-541c-b720-27ed7b24b2e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334126/selection/7a20def5811c2ee4e0f2a9977ea59d1a32d066cbcd86b924fdee15c4c0b08a64" :answer-field/choices ["q-334126/selection/c2c4bf203f1457c081aa67df90b16554bb5c4e724fe5cea01dd9dc527aee883c" "q-334126/selection/bfdc395819ce23330ffd2d6f3b03d819bbd0860f564964e1b7470932594ec907" "q-334126/selection/8d3e4dcc5745a1238e60616cb78b2a41cc363aa802ed60ae2d5c20912b398a6b" "q-334126/selection/bff161a2190bc6242a069ed224220089d10cb2d031d0e07863dd7f53bcda2984" "q-334126/selection/7a20def5811c2ee4e0f2a9977ea59d1a32d066cbcd86b924fdee15c4c0b08a64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334126" :question/id #uuid "75fa7e81-82d6-51b5-9f54-494e1c3e9275" :question/math-academy-id "q-334126" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -15 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above.\nFind the unknown function $f(t)$ in the general solution to the system, shown below.\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The matrix has the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+6\\text{i}$ with the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and associated eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -15 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe are given the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+6\\text{i}$ and the corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvector corresponding to the second eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}$ is \n${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}.$ But we do not require this eigenvector for solving our system.\n\nThe solution that we obtain for the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=4+6\\text{i}$ and its associated eigenvector is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(4+6\\text{i})t}.\n$$\n\nWe now express this as a real function. Using Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{(4+6\\text{i})t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)+\\text{i}{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)+2\\text{i}{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)-2{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)+\\text{i}{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t))+\\text{i}{e}^{4t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)) \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)+\\text{i}{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t} \\\\  & ={\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+\\text{i}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2}$ are linearly independent. Therefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{x}(t) & ={c}_{1}{\\text{w}}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{\\text{w}}_{2}(t) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334126/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3692fa3-14c5-5db9-8fee-e99ae35e386f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334126"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334132/selection/68abcb945b46be7858e218a58f2696e958f51fbe9f68877c5848b52106474f62" :answer/id #uuid "1a5f5b26-26f3-509a-a8f2-15b7158e094c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334132/selection/04ff119c3383fc895c3723f8bd8910600f3831f982acbfa7670270b9d85ded41" :answer/id #uuid "2f8092fa-ec29-5a5f-a16b-1b3d5c2f5ed2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334132/selection/